---@class remote.Company
---@field address_details any Fields can vary depending on the country. Please, check the required fields structure using the [Show form schema endpoint](#operation/get_show_form_country). Use the desired country and `address_details` as the form name for the placeholders. The response complies with the [JSON Schema](https://developer.remote.com/docs/how-json-schemas-work) specification.
---@field bank_account_details? any Fields can vary depending on the country. Please, check the required fields structure using the [Show form schema endpoint](#operation/get_show_form_country). Use the desired country and `bank_account_details` as the form name for the placeholders. The response complies with the [JSON Schema](https://developer.remote.com/docs/how-json-schemas-work) specification.
---@field company_owner_email string The email address of the company owner who administers the Remote account.
---@field company_owner_name? string The full name of the company owner. Cannot be changed after company creation.
---@field company_owner_user_id string The unique identifier (UUID) of the company owner's user account on Remote.
---@field country_code string The ISO 3166-1 3-letter country code where the company is registered.
---@field created_at string The timestamp when the company was created on Remote.
---@field default_legal_entity_credit_risk_status remote.CompanyDefaultLegalEntityCreditRiskStatus The credit risk status of the company default legal entity. - `not_started`: The credit risk assessment has not started yet. - `ready`: The credit risk assessment is ready to be started. - `in_progress`: The automated credit risk assessment is in progress. - `referred`: The credit risk assessment has been referred to a human reviewer. - `fail`: The credit risk assessment has failed and the company will be archived. - `deposit_required`: The company default legal entity requires a deposit before onboarding new employees. - `no_deposit_required`: The company default legal entity does not require a deposit before onboarding new employees.
---@field desired_currency string The ISO 4217 currency code the company prefers for billing and invoicing (e.g., "USD", "EUR").
---@field external_id? string|distilled.Null A unique reference code for this company in a non-Remote system. Null if not set.
---@field id string The unique identifier (UUID) of the company.
---@field name string The company's registered name. Can only be changed while the company is in `pending` status.
---@field phone_number? string The company's contact phone number.
---@field registration_number? string|distilled.Null The company's business registration number. Null if not provided. Can only be set while the company is in `pending` status.
---@field status remote.CompanyStatus The company status determines what a company is allowed to do: - `pending`: The company has been created and the company owner invited. Remote is waiting for the company owner to complete onboarding. - `review`: The company is under review. In rare occasions, a company may not automatically get created in `active` status because Remote needs to manually review the company that was created. The company will become `active` once the review is completed and no further action is necessary through the Remote API. - `active`: The company owner has completed onboarding and the company is ready to employ. - `archived`: The company is no longer active on the Remote platform and no changes can be made to the company.
---@field tax_number? string|distilled.Null The company's tax identification number. Null if not provided. Can only be set while the company is in `pending` status.
---@field terms_of_service_accepted_at string The timestamp when the company owner accepted Remote's Terms of Service.
---@field updated_at string The timestamp when the company record was last updated.

