---@class remote.CreateCompanyRequest
---@field address_details_json_schema_version? remote.CreateCompanyRequestAddressDetailsJsonSchemaVersion Version of the address_details form schema
---@field bank_account_details_json_schema_version? remote.CreateCompanyRequestBankAccountDetailsJsonSchemaVersion Version of the bank_account_details form schema
---@field action? string Complementary action(s) to perform when creating a company: - `get_oauth_access_tokens` returns the user's access and refresh tokens - `send_create_password_email ` sends a reset password token to the company owner's email so they can log in using Remote UI (not needed if integration plans to use SSO only) If `action` contains `send_create_password_email` you can redirect the user to [https://employ.remote.com/api-integration-new-password-send](https://employ.remote.com/api-integration-new-password-send)
---@field async? boolean Whether the request should be performed async
---@field scope? string Scope of the access token
---@field address_details? any Fields can vary depending on the country. Please, check the required fields structure using the [Show form schema endpoint](#operation/get_show_form_country). Use the desired country and `address_details` as the form name for the placeholders. The response complies with the [JSON Schema](https://developer.remote.com/docs/how-json-schemas-work) specification.
---@field bank_account_details? any Fields can vary depending on the country. Please, check the required fields structure using the [Show form schema endpoint](#operation/get_show_form_country). Use the desired country and `bank_account_details` as the form name for the placeholders. The response complies with the [JSON Schema](https://developer.remote.com/docs/how-json-schemas-work) specification.
---@field company_owner_email string The company owner email. This value cannot be changed once set.
---@field company_owner_name string The company owner name. This value cannot be changed from the Remote API once set.
---@field country_code string 3-letter country code of the country the company address is located in. For a list of countries supported through the Remote API, make a call to the [list countries endpoint](#tag/Countries/operation/get_supported_country). This endpoint will also include the 3-letter country codes you can use for this field.
---@field desired_currency remote.CreateCompanyRequestDesiredCurrency|string Desired currency for invoicing and displaying converted salaries in Remote UI regardless of the employee's country.
---@field email_domain? string The domain of the company. Use this field to specify the company domain name when it's different from the domain in the company owner's email.
---@field external_id? string Id of the company as represented in the external partner system.
---@field name string The company name
---@field phone_number? string A phone number the company can be contacted with.
---@field terms_of_service_accepted_at string Date and time the Terms of Service were accepted. To ensure users read the most recent version of Remote's Terms of Service, their action cannot have been done more than fifteen minutes ago. The UTC offset must be included in the ISO 8601 format: `YYYY-MM-DD HOURS:MINUTES:SECONDSZ`
---@field tax_number? string The tax identifier of the company. Exactly one of this field or `registration_number` must be submitted, not both.
---@field registration_number? string The company registration number. Exactly one of this field or `tax_number` must be submitted, not both.

---@alias remote.CreateCompanyRequestAddressDetailsJsonSchemaVersion number|remote.CreateCompanyRequestAddressDetailsJsonSchemaVersionCase1|string

---Use latest version
---@alias remote.CreateCompanyRequestAddressDetailsJsonSchemaVersionCase1 "latest"

---@alias remote.CreateCompanyRequestBankAccountDetailsJsonSchemaVersion number|remote.CreateCompanyRequestBankAccountDetailsJsonSchemaVersionCase1|string

