---Complete information of an employment, including all onboarding task statuses, country-specific form data (address, contract, administrative, etc.), and contractor-specific settings where applicable.
---@class remote.Employment
---@field personal_details any Personal details information. Its properties may vary depending on the country.
---@field short_id? string
---@field department? string|distilled.Null Name of related department, if any. Otherwise, null.
---@field manager_email string|distilled.Null The email address of the employee's manager. Null if no manager is assigned.
---@field provisional_start_date? string
---@field address_details any Home address information. Its properties may vary depending on the country.
---@field pricing_plan_details remote.PricingPlanDetails
---@field full_name string The employee's full name.
---@field partner_external_id? string|distilled.Null A reference code for the employment record in the calling integration's own system. Private to that integration — no other integration can read or overwrite it. Null when the integration has not set one. See [Your own IDs on Remote records](https://developer.remote.com/docs/your-own-ids-on-remote-records).
---@field type remote.EmploymentType For the employment types `contractor`, `global_payroll_employee` and `direct_employee`, only [List employments](#operation/get_index_employment) and [Show employment](#operation/get_show_employment) operations are available.
---@field contractor_settings? remote.EmploymentContractorSettings|distilled.Null Contractor-specific settings. Only present for contractor employments.
---@field employment_lifecycle_stage remote.EmploymentLifecycleStage
---@field administrative_details any Administrative information. Its properties may vary depending on the country.
---@field contractor_type? remote.EmploymentContractorType|distilled.Null Type of contractor product. Only present for contractor employments. 'standard' for Contractor Standard, 'cor' for Contractor of Record, 'plus' for Contractor Plus.
---@field contractor_rate? remote.EmploymentContractorRate|distilled.Null Contractor compensation rate details. Only present for contractor employments when rate is configured.
---@field company_id string The unique identifier (UUID) of the company this employment belongs to.
---@field expiration_date? string|distilled.Null The planned service end date for contractor of record (COR) employments. For signed COR contractors, this date is stored on the contract record (not in `contract_details`). It is `null` for employee employments or unsigned contractor agreements. Date format is ISO 8601 without the time component (e.g. "2024-12-31").
---@field work_address_details any Work address information. Its properties may vary depending on the country.
---@field bill_to_legal_entity_id? string|distilled.Null The unique identifier (UUID) of the legal entity that is billed for this employment.
---@field work_email string The employee's work email address, typically provided by the employer.
---@field status remote.EmploymentStatus
---@field updated_at string The timestamp when this employment record was last updated.
---@field has_active_withdrawal_method? boolean Whether the contractor has at least one active withdrawal method (the deposit method their invoices are paid out to). Only present for contractor employments. Use it to warn before creating an invoice schedule for a contractor who hasn't added one yet.
---@field basic_information? any Employment basic information. Its properties may vary depending on the country. When present, `login_email` indicates which address the employee logs in with: `"personal"` or `"work"`.
---@field job_title string|distilled.Null The employee's job title. May be null if not yet set.
---@field id string The unique identifier (UUID) of the employment.
---@field probation_period_end_date? string The date when the employee's probation period ends, if applicable.
---@field department_id? string|distilled.Null Unique ID of related department, if any. Otherwise, null.
---@field manager? string The full name of the employee's manager.
---@field login_email string The email address the employee uses to log in to the Remote platform.
---@field external_id? string|distilled.Null A unique reference code for the employment record in a non-Remote system. While uniqueness is recommended, it is not strictly enforced within Remote's system.
---@field employment_model remote.EmploymentEmploymentModel|distilled.Null For the employment models `peo` and `global_payroll`, only [List employments](#operation/get_index_employment) and [Show employment](#operation/get_show_employment) operations are available.
---@field personal_email string The employee's personal email address, used for account-related communications.
---@field country remote.NullableCountry|distilled.Null
---@field user_status? remote.UserStatus
---@field seniority_date? string
---@field bank_account_details remote.EmploymentBankAccountDetailsList
---@field files remote.EmploymentFilesList Documents associated with this employment (e.g., contracts, tax forms, identity documents).
---@field active_contract_id? string The unique identifier (UUID) of the currently active contract for this employment.
---@field engaged_by_legal_entity_id? string|distilled.Null The unique identifier (UUID) of the legal entity that engaged this employment.
---@field billing_address_details any Billing address information. Its properties may vary depending on the country.
---@field onboarding_tasks remote.OnboardingTasks
---@field contract_details any Contract information. Its properties may vary depending on the country.
---@field emergency_contact_details any Emergency contact information. Its properties may vary depending on the country.
---@field eligible_for_onboarding_cancellation boolean Whether this employment can still be cancelled during the onboarding process. Once the employment is active, this will be false.
---@field manager_employment_id string|distilled.Null The employment ID of the employee's manager on Remote, if the manager is also managed through Remote. Null otherwise.
---@field created_at string The timestamp when this employment record was created.

