---A file attached to the engagement agreement details.
---
---To upload a new file, send its `name` and its base64-encoded `content`. To keep a file uploaded
---previously, send back the `name` and `id` returned by the show endpoint instead. Every entry
---must do one or the other — an entry carrying neither is rejected, and an `id` that does not
---belong to this record is rejected too. Files that are not included in the payload are deleted.
---
---Only the properties below are accepted; any other one is rejected. In particular a file's
---`sub_type` is derived from the field it is attached to and cannot be set by the caller.
---@class remote.EngagementAgreementDetailsFileParams
---@field content? string The file content, Base64 encoded. Required when uploading a new file. The decoded content must match the extension given in `name`. Requests are capped at 25MB in total, which leaves room for a file of roughly 18MB once Base64 encoded.
---@field id? string ID of a file uploaded previously, as returned by the show endpoint. Send it to keep that file.
---@field name string The file name, including its extension.
---@field size? number The file size in bytes, before Base64 encoding.
---@field type? string The file's media type.

---@class remote.ErrorResponse
---@field details? string
---@field error? string

---A submitted expense record with complete data. All monetary amounts are integers in the currency's minor unit (cents).
---@class remote.Expense
---@field amount number The expense amount in the original currency, in cents.
---@field category? remote.ExpenseCategory|distilled.Null Categories allowed for an expense (legacy, deprecated)
---@field converted_amount number The expense amount converted to the company's billing currency, in cents.
---@field converted_currency remote.CurrencyDefinition
---@field converted_tax_amount number The tax portion converted to the company's billing currency, in cents.
---@field currency remote.CurrencyDefinition
---@field employment_id string The unique identifier (UUID) of the employment this expense belongs to.
---@field expense_category? remote.ExpenseExpenseCategory|distilled.Null New hierarchical expense category (recommended)
---@field expense_date string The date the expense was incurred (ISO 8601 format). Must be in the past.
---@field id string The unique identifier (UUID) of the expense.
---@field invoice_period? string|distilled.Null The payroll invoice period this expense is associated with, in YYYY-MM format. Null if not yet assigned to a payroll period.
---@field notes? string|distilled.Null Optional additional notes or context about the expense.
---@field project? remote.ExpenseProject|distilled.Null The company project the expense is tagged with. Null when it has none.
---@field reason? string|distilled.Null The reason provided when the expense was declined. Null for non-declined expenses.
---@field receipts? remote.ExpenseReceiptsList Uploaded receipt files for this expense. Maximum 5 receipts.
---@field reviewed_at? string|distilled.Null The date the expense was reviewed. Null if not yet reviewed.
---@field reviewer? remote.ExpenseReviewer|distilled.Null The person who reviewed (approved or declined) this expense. Null if not yet reviewed.
---@field status? remote.ExpenseStatus The current status of the expense. - `pending`: Submitted and awaiting approval. - `approved`: Approved by a reviewer and queued for reimbursement. - `declined`: Declined by a reviewer. See `reason` for details. - `canceled`: Canceled by the employee before approval. - `processing`: Being processed as part of a payroll run. - `reimbursed`: Successfully reimbursed to the employee.
---@field tax_amount number The tax portion of the expense amount in the original currency, in cents.
---@field title string A short description of the expense (e.g., "New keyboard", "Team dinner").

