---A feature flag that changes how the Remote API behaves, and whether it is on.
---@class remote.FeatureFlag
---@field applies_to remote.FeatureFlagAppliesTo `company`: the state is for the company in the path and can differ between companies. The other company flags are evaluated for the company admin the API acts as (the token's user, or the company owner for an integration token). The two `job_title_eligibility_check_*` flags are set per company instead. `environment`: the state is the same for every company in this environment.
---@field description string What the flag changes in the Remote API when it is on.
---@field enabled boolean Whether the API acts as if the flag is on, in Sandbox. It doesn't tell you the flag's state in production. For the two job title check flags, at most one is on: the check mode the company gets, which is off when its integration may skip the check.
---@field name string The flag's name. It doesn't change while the flag exists.

---`company`: the state is for the company in the path and can differ between companies. The other company flags are evaluated for the company admin the API acts as (the token's user, or the company owner for an integration token). The two `job_title_eligibility_check_*` flags are set per company instead. `environment`: the state is the same for every company in this environment.
---@alias remote.FeatureFlagAppliesTo "company"|"environment"

