---@class remote.GetEmploymentsRequest
---@field company_id? string Company ID
---@field email? string Filters the results by employments whose login email matches the value
---@field name? string Filters the results by the employee's name. Each whitespace-separated word is matched partially, ignoring casing and accents, so `grace hop` matches "Gráce Brewster Murray Hopper".
---@field status? string Filters the results by employments whose status matches the value. Supports multiple values separated by commas. Also supports the value `incomplete` to get all employments that are not onboarded yet. Allowed values: `active`, `created`, `created_awaiting_reserve`, `created_reserve_paid`, `initiated`, `invited`, `pending`, `pre_hire`, `review`, `job_title_review`, `pending_post_self_enrollment_actions`, `archived`, `incomplete`. Any other value returns a `422`. Offboarded employments have the status `archived`.
---@field employment_type? string Filters the results by employments whose employment product type matches the value
---@field employment_model? remote.GetEmploymentsRequestEmploymentModel|string Filters the results by employments whose employment model matches the value. Possible values: `global_payroll`, `peo`, `eor`
---@field short_id? string Filters the results by the employment's short ID. Returns at most one result.
---@field partner_external_id? string Filters the results by the `partner_external_id` value the calling integration holds for the employment; another integration's identifiers are never matched. Matching is exact, including case. The same value may be set on several employments (for example a rehire), so several results may be returned. See [Your own IDs on Remote records](https://developer.remote.com/docs/your-own-ids-on-remote-records).
---@field page? number Starts fetching records after the given page
---@field page_size? number Number of items per page

---@alias remote.GetEmploymentsRequestEmploymentModel "global_payroll"|"peo"|"eor"

