---@class remote.PayItem
---@field amount number Value of the pay item. Its unit depends on the `type` of the pay code (see GET /v1/companies/:company_id/legal-entities/:legal_entity_id/pay-codes): `amount` in cents, `percentage` in basis points, `unit` as a raw count, `hours` as a whole number of hours, `duration` in seconds.
---@field code string Pay item type code
---@field custom_configuration? remote.PayItemCustomConfiguration|distilled.Null
---@field effective_date string Date the pay item is applied on (YYYY-MM-DD) — the day worked, the day a correction was submitted, or the first day of a leave period.
---@field employment_id string Employment UUID
---@field end_date string|distilled.Null Last day of a leave period, inclusive (YYYY-MM-DD). Only for Leave-of-absence pay codes; Leave empty for other pay codes.
---@field id string Pay item's unique identifier. Editing `amount` or `effective_date` creates a new version with a new `id`; every `id` this API returned for a pay item edited through `PATCH` keeps working on `PATCH` and `DELETE` and resolves to the current version, except for a payment generated from a recurring pay item, which returns 422.
---@field partner_external_id? string|distilled.Null A reference code for the pay item record in the calling integration's own system. Private to that integration — no other integration can read or overwrite it. Null when the integration has not set one. See [Your own IDs on Remote records](https://developer.remote.com/docs/your-own-ids-on-remote-records).
---@field provider_data remote.PayItemProviderData
---@field replaced_ids remote.PayItemReplacedIdsList Earlier `id`s of this pay item, oldest first; empty if it has never been edited. Each of them still resolves to the current version on `PATCH` and `DELETE`, so tracking them is strongly advised but not necessary.

---@class remote.PayItemBulkCreateFailureDetail
---@field code string Stable, machine-parseable failure reason.
---@field message string Human-readable detail for the failure reason.
---@field param? string Slash-separated path of the field at fault, e.g. `custom_configuration/values/make`.

---@class remote.PayItemBulkCreateFailures
---@field error? remote.PayItemBulkCreateFailuresError Failure reason. Includes `employment_not_global_payroll` when the provided employment is not Global Payroll, `pay_item_code_not_allowed` / `pay_item_external_import_code_not_allowed` when the given identifier does not resolve to an allowed pay element, and `effective_date_after_termination_date` (as a `code`/`message` pair) when a `time_attendance` pay item's `effective_date` falls after the employment's termination date. It also includes `custom_configuration_required`, `custom_configuration_not_used` and `invalid_custom_configuration` (as `code`/`message`/`param`) when the pay item's `custom_configuration` doesn't match the pay code's. An item with a `partner_external_id` can also fail with `partner_external_id_not_available`, `partner_external_id_blank`, `partner_external_id_repeated_in_request`, `partner_external_id_ambiguous`, `partner_external_id_held_by_other_pay_item` or `partner_external_id_held_by_generated_pay_item` (as `code`/`message`), with the errors `PATCH` returns when the matched pay item cannot be updated, or with `errors.partner_external_id` when the value is refused.
---@field row_number? number

---Failure reason. Includes `employment_not_global_payroll` when the provided employment is not Global Payroll, `pay_item_code_not_allowed` / `pay_item_external_import_code_not_allowed` when the given identifier does not resolve to an allowed pay element, and `effective_date_after_termination_date` (as a `code`/`message` pair) when a `time_attendance` pay item's `effective_date` falls after the employment's termination date. It also includes `custom_configuration_required`, `custom_configuration_not_used` and `invalid_custom_configuration` (as `code`/`message`/`param`) when the pay item's `custom_configuration` doesn't match the pay code's. An item with a `partner_external_id` can also fail with `partner_external_id_not_available`, `partner_external_id_blank`, `partner_external_id_repeated_in_request`, `partner_external_id_ambiguous`, `partner_external_id_held_by_other_pay_item` or `partner_external_id_held_by_generated_pay_item` (as `code`/`message`), with the errors `PATCH` returns when the matched pay item cannot be updated, or with `errors.partner_external_id` when the value is refused.
---@alias remote.PayItemBulkCreateFailuresError string|remote.PayItemBulkCreateFailureDetail|remote.PayItemBulkCreateFailuresErrorCase2

---@class remote.PayItemBulkCreateFailuresErrorCase2
