---@class remote.PayItemBulkCreateSuccesses
---@field pay_item remote.PayItem
---@field row_number number

---The pay item custom configuration values for pay codes that use one, such as the employee's company car. The pay code's `custom_configuration` (GET …/pay-codes) gives the `key` and the JSON Schema of the `values`. On PATCH, `values` are merged onto the stored ones: nested objects merge, and `null` removes a field at any level. Send `null` for the whole `custom_configuration` to remove the stored values.
---@class remote.PayItemCustomConfiguration
---@field key string The pay code's `custom_configuration.key`
---@field values any Values matching the pay code's `custom_configuration.schema`

---@class remote.PayItemParams
---@field amount number Value of the pay item. Its unit depends on the `type` of the pay code (see GET /v1/companies/:company_id/legal-entities/:legal_entity_id/pay-codes): `amount` in cents, `percentage` in basis points, `unit` as a raw count, `hours` as a whole number of hours, `duration` in seconds. Must not be zero. **Negative values are supported.** A positive `amount` adds value; a negative `amount` takes value away. Send a negative `amount` to submit a deduction, or to correct an earlier submission downwards. This applies to every pay code, whatever its unit — including hours-based codes such as `working_hours`. For example: - `-5000` on an `amount` code (cents) deducts 50.00 from pay. - `-3` on an hours-based code such as `working_hours` removes 3 hours reported in error.
---@field code? string Pay item type code. Mutually exclusive with `external_import_code` — provide exactly one.
---@field currency? string|distilled.Null
---@field custom_configuration? remote.PayItemCustomConfiguration|distilled.Null
---@field effective_date string Date the pay item is applied on (YYYY-MM-DD). For an original submission this is the day worked; for a correction it is the day the correction is submitted, so the pay item lands in the right payroll run. The day being corrected goes in `provider_data.correction_effective_date`. On a leave-of-absence pay item this is the first day of the leave period, whose last day goes in `end_date`.
---@field employment_id string Employment UUID. Only Global Payroll employments are supported.
---@field end_date? string|distilled.Null Last day of a leave period, inclusive (YYYY-MM-DD). Set this only on leave-of-absence pay codes — parental, sick, maternity, unpaid leave and similar — where the pay item covers a period rather than a single day, and `effective_date` is the first day of that period. Leave it off ordinary time & attendance items such as worked hours, overtime or allowances, which apply to a single day.
---@field external_import_code? string Partner-defined pay element identifier, as configured on the legal entity pay element. Mutually exclusive with `code` — provide exactly one.
---@field partner_external_id? string|distilled.Null A reference code for the pay item record in the calling integration's own system. Private to that integration — no other integration can read or overwrite it. When the integration already holds this value on a live pay item, the item updates that pay item; otherwise it creates a new pay item holding the value. `null` or an empty string fails the item. An item without the field always creates a new pay item, so sending it again creates a duplicate. At most 64 characters, counting any surrounding whitespace sent; that whitespace is then trimmed off. A value can be held by one live pay item at a time, per integration and company; editing a pay item keeps its value on the new version. See [Your own IDs on Remote records](https://developer.remote.com/docs/your-own-ids-on-remote-records).
---@field provider_data? remote.PayItemProviderDataParams

---@class remote.PayItemProviderData
---@field correction_effective_date? string Set this only on a correction: the original working day being corrected (YYYY-MM-DD). Its presence is what marks the pay item as a correction rather than an original submission.
---@field hourly_rate? number Hourly rate in cents
---@field hourly_rate_currency_code? string
---@field pay_rate? number Overtime rate multiplier (e.g. 1.5)
---@field shift_code? string Shift identifier from partner system
---@field work_day_duration? number Expected work day duration in seconds

---@class remote.PayItemProviderDataParams
---@field adjustment_effective_date? string **Deprecated — renamed to `correction_effective_date`**, which this value backfills. `correction_effective_date` wins when both are sent.
---@field correction_effective_date? string Set this only on a correction: the original working day being corrected (YYYY-MM-DD). Its presence is what marks the pay item as a correction rather than an original submission.
---@field hourly_rate? number Hourly rate in cents
---@field hourly_rate_currency_code? string|distilled.Null
---@field is_deduction? boolean **Deprecated — accepted and ignored.** Express a deduction as a negative `amount`.
---@field pay_rate? number Overtime rate multiplier (e.g. 1.5)
---@field payout_amount? number **Deprecated — accepted and ignored.** The payout value belongs in the pay item's own `amount`.
---@field payout_currency_code? string **Deprecated — accepted and ignored.** The payout currency belongs in the pay item's own `currency`.
---@field shift_code? string Shift identifier from partner system
---@field work_day_duration? number Expected work day duration in seconds

