---A payroll run represents a single payroll processing cycle for a company in a specific country and period. It progresses through statuses from preparation to finalization, and contains cost totals aggregated across all employees included in the run.
---@class remote.PayrollRun
---@field approval_date string|distilled.Null
---@field benefits_total number The total benefits cost across all employees in this payroll run. Amount in cents.
---@field country remote.Country
---@field currency_code string
---@field cutoff_date? string|distilled.Null
---@field employee_details remote.PayrollRunEmployeeDetailsList Per-employee cost breakdown for this payroll run. Deprecated — use the dedicated `GET /v1/payroll-runs/{payroll_run_id}/employee-details` endpoint instead, which supports pagination.
---@field employer_contributions_total number The total employer-side contributions (social contributions, employer taxes, etc.) across all employees. Amount in cents.
---@field expected_payout_date string
---@field expenses_total number The total reimbursed expenses across all employees in this payroll run. Amount in cents.
---@field id string The unique identifier of the payroll run.
---@field incentives_total number The total incentives (bonuses, commissions, etc.) across all employees in this payroll run. Amount in cents.
---@field other_total number The total of other payroll components not categorized elsewhere. Amount in cents.
---@field period_end string
---@field period_start string
---@field salary_total number The total base salary amount across all employees in this payroll run. Amount in cents.
---@field status remote.PayrollRunStatus The current status of the payroll run. - `preparing`: The payroll run is being assembled. Employee details and costs are estimates and may change. - `processing`: The payroll run has been submitted for processing by the local payroll provider. Costs are still estimates. - `completed`: Payroll processing is complete. Costs are final and payslips are available. - `finalized`: The payroll run has been finalized and payments have been or will be disbursed. - `waiting_for_customer_approval`: The payroll run requires approval from the company before it can proceed. - `rejected`: The payroll run was rejected during the approval process and needs to be revised.
---@field total_payroll_cost number The total cost of this payroll run across all employees, including salaries, benefits, employer contributions, expenses, and incentives. Amount in cents.
---@field type? remote.PayrollRunType The type of payroll run. - `main`: The regular recurring payroll for the period. - `one_off`: An ad-hoc payroll run outside the regular cycle, typically for off-cycle payments. - `pro_forma`: A simulated payroll run used for cost estimation purposes. Not actually processed. - `tax_documents`: A payroll run for generating tax-related documents only. - `year_end_reports`: A year-end run holding employees' year-end tax documents (e.g. T4, RL-1). - `employer_year_end_reports`: A year-end run holding company-level reports for the employer to review and approve. Global Payroll only. - `expenses`: A payroll run dedicated to reimbursing approved expenses. - `parallel`: A supplementary payroll run that runs alongside the main payroll for the same period.

---Per-employee cost breakdown for this payroll run. Deprecated — use the dedicated `GET /v1/payroll-runs/{payroll_run_id}/employee-details` endpoint instead, which supports pagination.
---@alias remote.PayrollRunEmployeeDetailsList remote.EmployeeDetails[]

---Response containing a single payroll run with full details including cost totals and employee breakdowns.
---@class remote.PayrollRunResponse
---@field payroll_run? remote.PayrollRun

---The current status of the payroll run.
---
---- `preparing`: The payroll run is being assembled. Employee details and costs are estimates and may change.
---- `processing`: The payroll run has been submitted for processing by the local payroll provider. Costs are still estimates.
---- `completed`: Payroll processing is complete. Costs are final and payslips are available.
---- `finalized`: The payroll run has been finalized and payments have been or will be disbursed.
---- `waiting_for_customer_approval`: The payroll run requires approval from the company before it can proceed.
---- `rejected`: The payroll run was rejected during the approval process and needs to be revised.
---@alias remote.PayrollRunStatus "preparing"|"processing"|"completed"|"finalized"|"waiting_for_customer_approval"|"rejected"

---The type of payroll run.
---
---- `main`: The regular recurring payroll for the period.
---- `one_off`: An ad-hoc payroll run outside the regular cycle, typically for off-cycle payments.
---- `pro_forma`: A simulated payroll run used for cost estimation purposes. Not actually processed.
---- `tax_documents`: A payroll run for generating tax-related documents only.
---- `year_end_reports`: A year-end run holding employees' year-end tax documents (e.g. T4, RL-1).
---- `employer_year_end_reports`: A year-end run holding company-level reports for the employer to review and approve. Global Payroll only.
---- `expenses`: A payroll run dedicated to reimbursing approved expenses.
---- `parallel`: A supplementary payroll run that runs alongside the main payroll for the same period.
---@alias remote.PayrollRunType "main"|"one_off"|"pro_forma"|"tax_documents"|"year_end_reports"|"employer_year_end_reports"|"expenses"|"parallel"

