---Resignation details for an employee who resigned after their employment start date. Includes contract terms, notice period calculations, and PTO breakdown needed for the employer to validate the resignation.
---@class remote.ResignationAfterStartDate
---@field contract_currency_code string The ISO 4217 currency code of the employee's contract (used for any reimbursement calculations).
---@field contract_job_title string The job title from the employee's contract.
---@field contract_proabtion_period_passed boolean Whether the employee's probation period has passed. Affects notice period requirements in many jurisdictions.
---@field contract_probation_period_end_date string|distilled.Null The end date of the employee's probation period. Null if the contract has no probation period.
---@field contract_start_date string The original start date from the employee's contract.
---@field days_of_notice number The number of calendar days of notice required based on the contract terms and local labor laws.
---@field paid_timeoffs_breakdown_labels remote.ResignationAfterStartDatePaidTimeoffsBreakdownLabelsList Human-readable breakdown of the employee's paid time off usage and balance (e.g., "Used until today: 60 days", "Waiting for approval: 0 days").
---@field proposed_last_day string The employee's proposed last working day, calculated based on the notice period and local labor laws.
---@field resignation_date string The date the employee submitted their resignation (UTC).
---@field resignation_reason_label string A human-readable label describing the reason for resignation (e.g., "Retirement", "Other job opportunity").

---Human-readable breakdown of the employee's paid time off usage and balance (e.g., "Used until today: 60 days", "Waiting for approval: 0 days").
---@alias remote.ResignationAfterStartDatePaidTimeoffsBreakdownLabelsList string[]

---@class remote.ResignationAfterStartDateRequestParams
---@field accepts_proposed_notice boolean Whether the employer accepts the proposed notice period and last working day. If false, provide an alternative `proposed_last_date`.
---@field agrees_to_pto_amount boolean Whether the employer agrees with the employee's current PTO balance. If false, provide notes explaining the discrepancy.
---@field agrees_to_pto_amount_notes? string Required if `agrees_to_pto_amount` is set to false.
---@field agrees_to_resignation_reason boolean Whether the employer agrees with the resignation reason stated by the employee. If false, provide notes with the employer's perspective.
---@field agrees_to_resignation_reason_notes? string required if `agrees_to_resignation_reason` is set to false.
---@field has_additional_information boolean Whether the employer has additional information to share about the resignation. If true, provide notes.
---@field has_additional_information_notes? string required if `has_additional_information` is set to true.
---@field has_more_salary_info boolean Whether there are salary adjustments or additional salary information to communicate. If true, provide notes.
---@field has_more_salary_info_notes? string required if `has_more_salary_info` is set to true.
---@field is_owed_outstanding_reimbursements boolean Whether the employee is owed any outstanding expense reimbursements. If true, provide the amount and notes.
---@field owed_outstanding_reimbursements? remote.ResignationAfterStartDateRequestParamsOwedOutstandingReimbursements required if `is_owed_outstanding_reimbursements` is set to true.
---@field proposed_last_date? remote.ResignationAfterStartDateRequestParamsProposedLastDate Required if `accepts_proposed_notice` is set to false.
---@field timesheet_file? remote.ResignationFile Paid time off accuracy Typically, any vacation pay accrued and unpaid at the time of termination must be paid out to the employee. To avoid overpaying or underpaying, please make sure we have an accurate account of their paid time off by querying the [Show Time Off Balance](#operation/get_show_timeoff_balance) endpoint, filtering by the `employment_id`. This optional document should be sent in case of any discrepancies.
---@field will_take_more_pto boolean Whether the employee intends to take more PTO before their last working day. If true, provide notes with details.
---@field will_take_more_pto_notes? string required if `will_take_more_pto` is set to true.

---required if `is_owed_outstanding_reimbursements` is set to true.
---@class remote.ResignationAfterStartDateRequestParamsOwedOutstandingReimbursements
---@field amount? number The amount (in the currency of the employment) to be given to the employee. This field accepts fractional amounts as well. However to avoid precision issues and errors that can arise from storing fractional amounts, the Remote API only accepts currencies and their fractional amounts as integers. This means you should append fractional amounts to the end of the amount you're passing in with this field. For example, if the amount you're offering is EUR 500.25, you would specify `50025` as the amount for this field.
---@field notes? string

---Required if `accepts_proposed_notice` is set to false.
---@class remote.ResignationAfterStartDateRequestParamsProposedLastDate
---@field date? string
---@field notes? string

