---A travel letter request submitted by an employee who needs a formal letter from their employer to support a visa or travel application. The request goes through a two-stage approval: first by the employer manager, then by Remote.
---@class remote.TravelLetterRequest
---@field additional_information string Additional information provided by the employee about their travel plans.
---@field destination_country remote.Country
---@field embassy_address string The address of the embassy or consulate where the travel letter will be submitted.
---@field employer_approver remote.TravelLetterUser|distilled.Null
---@field employer_special_instructions string|distilled.Null Special instructions from the employer to include in the travel letter. Null if none provided.
---@field id string The unique identifier (UUID) of the travel letter request.
---@field reason string The purpose of the travel (e.g., business meeting, conference, client visit).
---@field requires_travel_address boolean Whether the employee needs to provide a specific travel address (accommodation address at the destination).
---@field responsible_for_accommodation_cost remote.TravelLetterRequestResponsibleForAccommodationCost|distilled.Null Who is responsible for accommodation costs during the trip. Set by the employer during approval. Null if not yet approved.
---@field responsible_for_meal_cost remote.TravelLetterRequestResponsibleForMealCost|distilled.Null Who is responsible for meal costs during the trip. Set by the employer during approval. Null if not yet approved.
---@field responsible_for_travel_cost remote.TravelLetterRequestResponsibleForTravelCost|distilled.Null Who is responsible for transportation costs. Set by the employer during approval. Null if not yet approved.
---@field status remote.TravelLetterRequestStatus The current status of the travel letter request. - `pending`: Submitted by the employee and awaiting manager review. - `cancelled`: Cancelled by the employee before approval. - `declined_by_manager`: The employer manager declined the request. - `declined_by_remote`: Remote declined the request after manager approval (e.g., compliance reasons). - `approved_by_manager`: Approved by the employer manager, awaiting Remote's review. - `approved_by_remote`: Fully approved by both the manager and Remote. The travel letter will be generated.
---@field submitted_at string
---@field travel_address string|distilled.Null The employee's accommodation address at the destination. Null if `requires_travel_address` is false or not yet provided.
---@field travel_date_end string
---@field travel_date_start string
---@field travel_document_number string The employee's travel document (passport) number.
---@field travel_reason string The category of travel reason selected by the employee.
---@field travel_reason_details string Detailed explanation of the travel reason provided by the employee.
---@field user remote.TravelLetterUser|distilled.Null

---Who is responsible for accommodation costs during the trip. Set by the employer during approval. Null if not yet approved.
---@alias remote.TravelLetterRequestResponsibleForAccommodationCost "employee"|"employer"

---Who is responsible for meal costs during the trip. Set by the employer during approval. Null if not yet approved.
---@alias remote.TravelLetterRequestResponsibleForMealCost "employee"|"employer"

---Who is responsible for transportation costs. Set by the employer during approval. Null if not yet approved.
---@alias remote.TravelLetterRequestResponsibleForTravelCost "employee"|"employer"

---The current status of the travel letter request.
---
---- `pending`: Submitted by the employee and awaiting manager review.
---- `cancelled`: Cancelled by the employee before approval.
---- `declined_by_manager`: The employer manager declined the request.
---- `declined_by_remote`: Remote declined the request after manager approval (e.g., compliance reasons).
---- `approved_by_manager`: Approved by the employer manager, awaiting Remote's review.
---- `approved_by_remote`: Fully approved by both the manager and Remote. The travel letter will be generated.
---@alias remote.TravelLetterRequestStatus "pending"|"cancelled"|"declined_by_manager"|"declined_by_remote"|"approved_by_manager"|"approved_by_remote"

