---Bulk Create Pay Items
---
---Bulk creates pay items for employments. Supports up to 500 items per request.
---Each item must supply exactly one of `code` or `external_import_code` to identify the pay element.
---Integration-specific fields (shift code, currency, pay amount, etc.) go in the `provider_data` object.
---Pay codes that use a pay item custom configuration, such as a company car, describe it under `custom_configuration` in GET /v1/companies/:company_id/legal-entities/:legal_entity_id/pay-codes. Send its values in the pay item's `custom_configuration`, with the same `key`.
---Only Global Payroll employments are supported. Non-GP employments are returned as `employment_not_global_payroll`.
---An item whose `partner_external_id` the integration already holds on a live pay item of the company updates that pay item under the same rules as `PATCH`, and any other item creates a new pay item.
---When that pay item belongs to another employment or pay code, the item fails with `partner_external_id_held_by_other_pay_item` instead.
---When pay items generated from a recurring pay item hold the value, the item fails with `partner_external_id_held_by_generated_pay_item`, naming them. Clear its `partner_external_id` with `PATCH` to use the value again; when it has more than one live version, contact Remote support.
---When more than one live pay item holds the value, the item fails with `partner_external_id_ambiguous`, unless it already fails for its employment or its pay code, or because the value is held by a recurring pay item or a payment generated from one.
---Within one request each `partner_external_id` may appear once, and `null` or an empty string fails the item.
---An item without `partner_external_id` always creates a new pay item, so sending it again creates a duplicate.
---See [Your own IDs on Remote records](https://developer.remote.com/docs/your-own-ids-on-remote-records).
---
---## Authentication
---
---This endpoint accepts any one of the following token types:
---
---- **Company-scoped access token** (`OAuth2AuthorizationCode`) — obtained by a company manager through the Authorization Code flow or the Refresh Token flow. See [Authentication for partners](https://developer.remote.com/docs/authentication-for-partners).
---- **Company-scoped access token (assertion)** (`OAuth2CompanyManagerAssertion`) — obtained through the `urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:jwt-bearer` grant for a company manager. See [OAuth Assertion](https://developer.remote.com/docs/authorization-method-oauth-assertion).
---- **Customer API token** (`CustomerAPIToken`) — generated by the customer on their Integration Settings page, with the scopes they choose there. See [Authorization for customers](https://developer.remote.com/docs/authorization-for-customers).
---
---## Scopes
---
---Any one of the scopes in a token type's row is enough. `all:write` works too.
---
---`POST /v1/pay-items/bulk`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, Conflict, UnprocessableEntity.
---@param input remote.CreatePayItemsBulkRequest
---@return remote.BulkCreatePayItemsResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:create_pay_items_bulk(input) end

