---Update a Pay Item
---
---Updates a pay item. Only the fields provided are changed. Editing `amount` or `effective_date` archives the existing pay item and creates a new one with a new `id`. Any `id` this API returned for a pay item edited through `PATCH`, including every entry of `replaced_ids`, keeps working and resolves to its current version (except for payments generated from a recurring pay item, which return 422), so storing the new id is strongly advised but not necessary; `replaced_ids` in the response lists the earlier ids for integrations that track changes. A deleted pay item (no live version left) returns 404 with the message "Pay item not found because it was deleted". A deleted payment generated from a recurring pay item returns 422 instead, unless the request only clears `partner_external_id`.
---Send `partner_external_id` to set or change the calling integration's own reference code, or `null` or an empty string to clear it. An edit that creates a new `id` keeps the value on the new version.
---See [Your own IDs on Remote records](https://developer.remote.com/docs/your-own-ids-on-remote-records).
---Cannot update pay items linked to a payroll adjustment, salary pay items, pay items automatically created from an external source, pay items whose payroll run is no longer in preparation, or pay items with more than one live version.
---The one change allowed on a pay item linked to a payroll adjustment, a salary pay item, one created from an external source, a payment generated from a recurring pay item or one whose payroll run is no longer in preparation is clearing `partner_external_id`: a request whose only field is `partner_external_id`, sent as `null` or an empty string, clears it and leaves the pay item itself unchanged. Setting a value on such a pay item is refused, so the clear can't be undone, and a bulk item sent again with the cleared value creates a new pay item. A clear still gets the not found, recurring, more than one live version and "is not available" refusals; any pay item they allow accepts it, including one dated after the employment's termination date.
---Recurring pay items cannot be updated or deleted through this API and return 422, and neither can the payments generated from them, except to clear `partner_external_id`.
---When more than one refusal applies, the first in this order is returned: an employment that isn't on Global Payroll (404 "Pay item not found"), a recurring pay item or a payment generated from one (422), then a pay item with more than one live version (422).
---When `custom_configuration` doesn't match the pay code's custom configuration, the 422 response is a parameter error with the same `code` bulk create returns: `custom_configuration_not_used`, `custom_configuration_required` or `invalid_custom_configuration`, and the `param` at fault.
---
---## Authentication
---
---This endpoint accepts any one of the following token types:
---
---- **Company-scoped access token** (`OAuth2AuthorizationCode`) — obtained by a company manager through the Authorization Code flow or the Refresh Token flow. See [Authentication for partners](https://developer.remote.com/docs/authentication-for-partners).
---- **Company-scoped access token (assertion)** (`OAuth2CompanyManagerAssertion`) — obtained through the `urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:jwt-bearer` grant for a company manager. See [OAuth Assertion](https://developer.remote.com/docs/authorization-method-oauth-assertion).
---- **Customer API token** (`CustomerAPIToken`) — generated by the customer on their Integration Settings page, with the scopes they choose there. See [Authorization for customers](https://developer.remote.com/docs/authorization-for-customers).
---
---## Scopes
---
---Any one of the scopes in a token type's row is enough. `all:write` works too.
---
---`PATCH /v1/pay-items/{id}`
---Errors: BadRequest, Forbidden, NotFound, Conflict, UnprocessableEntity.
---@param input remote.UpdatePayItemRequest
---@return remote.PayItemResponse? value
---@return distilled.Error? err
function Client:update_pay_item(input) end

